Viewer: fixes from testing against the F50 and a second review (2026-10-12).

- A realignment queues the unheard seconds again (up to 5 s); the "music buffer is not advancing" limit was
  12 fragments for FLAC (1 s) and closed the music. Now 80 fragments (6.8 s) for AAC and FLAC alike.
- No realignment while the music element is paused (not unlocked yet, or the car gave the sound to another
  app); it aligns when it plays again instead of reshuffling the buffer every 5 s.
- Resuming never steps back: after a pause the buffer may be played out, and going 1 s back replayed what was
  heard. The element now waits for a cushion of new audio and plays on.
- Fullscreen: Chrome tells a hidden page it left fullscreen only once the page is shown again (hidden, shown,
  then out of fullscreen), which looked like leaving on purpose and renegotiated the picture. An exit within
  2 s of being shown after the page was covered in fullscreen now counts as covered. A pending decision is
  dropped when fullscreen changes again, and leaving on purpose fits the window afterwards.
- No renegotiation while the page is hidden or waits for its fullscreen tap: a resize timer set just before the
  page was covered fired while hidden and renegotiated to the small size Chrome reports then.
Headless Chrome against the F50 with an iPhone in CarPlay, three runs: hidden for 2.5 s before the exit, and
leaving fullscreen on purpose then re-entering before the car covers the page: the hint shows, one tap goes back
to fullscreen, the tap does not reach CarPlay, and no renegotiation after the first fullscreen.

